<div class="sa-shell">
  <section class="sa-section">
    <h2>Scene Architect</h2>
    <p>Create one illustrated map, then refine its editable Foundry walls and doors.</p>
    <div class="sa-actions sa-wrap">
      <select name="projectId" aria-label="Saved Scene Architect scene"><option value="">Choose saved scene…</option>{{#each projects}}<option value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{name}}</option>{{/each}}</select>
      <button type="button" data-action="reopen">Reopen</button>
      <button type="button" data-action="newProject">New project</button>
      <button type="button" data-action="loadExample">Load laboratory example</button>
    </div>
    {{#if sceneReady}}<p class="sa-status good">Working scene: <strong>{{sceneNameLinked}}</strong></p>{{/if}}
    {{#if editedGeometry}}<p class="sa-status warning">Native geometry or scene settings differ from the original plan. Manual wall and door edits are supported and preserved. The overlay uses your current walls; reference room labels and feature positions still come from the saved plan.</p>{{/if}}
    {{#if legacyTiles}}<p class="sa-status warning">This scene has {{legacyTiles}} older generated prop Tiles. They stay above any imported map. Build a new scene from the plan for a clean start, or remove unwanted Tiles in Foundry.</p>{{/if}}
  </section>
  <section class="sa-section">
    <details {{#unless hasPlan}}open{{/unless}}>
      <summary>1. Describe and plan the map</summary>
      <div class="sa-grid sa-grid-4">
        <label>Scene name<input name="sceneName" value="{{sceneName}}"></label>
        <label>Columns<input type="number" name="columns" min="4" max="200" value="{{columns}}"></label>
        <label>Rows<input type="number" name="rows" min="4" max="200" value="{{rows}}"></label>
        <label>Grid px<input type="number" name="gridSize" min="50" max="400" value="{{gridSize}}"></label>
      </div>
      <label>Describe the map<textarea name="brief" rows="5">{{brief}}</textarea></label>
      <p class="hint">Copy the layout request to ChatGPT, then import the returned JSON. Or load the laboratory example above.</p>
      <div class="sa-actions"><button type="button" data-action="copyLayoutPrompt">Copy layout request</button><button type="button" data-action="pastePlan">Import / edit plan JSON</button></div>
    </details>
    {{#if hasPlan}}
      <p class="sa-status good">{{planSummary}}</p>
      {{#each warnings}}<p class="sa-status warning">{{this}}</p>{{/each}}
      <div class="sa-actions sa-wrap">
        <button type="button" data-action="buildDraft">{{#if sceneReady}}Build a new scene from plan{{else}}Build draft scene{{/if}}</button>
        <button type="button" data-action="downloadPlan">Download original plan JSON</button>
        {{#if sceneReady}}<button type="button" data-action="viewScene">View scene</button>{{/if}}
      </div>
      <details><summary>Inspect original plan</summary><p class="hint">Native edits are saved by Foundry, not written back into this JSON.</p><pre>{{planJson}}</pre></details>
    {{/if}}
  </section>
  {{#if sceneReady}}
  <section class="sa-section">
    <h2>2. Generate one complete map</h2>
    <p>Export the PNG reference and attach it in ChatGPT with the copied map prompt. Generate and download one complete map image.</p>
    <p class="hint">The reference guides architecture and composition. Artwork can flow across grid boundaries. Image generation may shift walls or doors; expect to review and adjust them in Foundry.</p>
    <div class="sa-actions"><button type="button" data-action="exportGuide">Export PNG reference</button><button type="button" data-action="copyMapPrompt">Copy map prompt</button></div>
  </section>
  <section class="sa-section">
    <h2>3. Import and align the map</h2>
    <label>Complete map image (PNG, JPEG or WebP, up to 30 MB)<input type="file" name="mapFile" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp"></label>
    {{#if mapSource}}<p class="hint">Saved source: {{mapSource}}. Leave the file empty to reuse it.</p>{{/if}}
    <p class="hint">The full image initially fits the scene's full rectangle. A different aspect ratio will stretch. Scale is centred; positive offsets move the image right/down. Preview again after changing values. Settings save when you apply.</p>
    <div class="sa-grid sa-grid-3">
      <label>Scale (%)<input name="mapScale" type="number" min="10" max="400" step="1" value="{{scale}}"></label>
      <label>Horizontal offset (px)<input name="mapX" type="number" min="-8192" max="8192" value="{{offsetX}}"></label>
      <label>Vertical offset (px)<input name="mapY" type="number" min="-8192" max="8192" value="{{offsetY}}"></label>
    </div>
    <label class="sa-check"><input name="showWalls" type="checkbox" checked> Show live walls and doors in preview</label>
    <p class="hint">Yellow: walls · Blue: doors · Purple: secret doors. The overlay is never baked into your map.</p>
    <p class="sa-map-warning sa-status warning" role="status"></p>
    <div class="sa-actions"><button type="button" data-action="previewMap">Preview alignment</button><button type="button" data-action="applyMap">Apply map background</button></div>
    <div class="sa-map-preview"></div>
  </section>
  <section class="sa-section">
    <h2>4. Optional: fit geometry to the finished artwork</h2>
    <p>After applying your map background, export a clean analysis image and attach it to ChatGPT with the analysis prompt. Paste or upload the returned geometry JSON below.</p>
    <p class="hint">Use this exported image, which includes your applied scale and position. Ask ChatGPT to analyse it in a separate follow-up after generation. No API connection is used.</p>
    {{#if analysisReady}}
    <div class="sa-actions sa-wrap"><button type="button" data-action="exportAnalysisImage">Export analysis image</button><button type="button" data-action="copyAnalysisPrompt">Copy analysis prompt</button></div>
    {{#if analysisWarning}}<p class="sa-status warning">{{analysisWarning}}</p>{{/if}}
    <label>Geometry JSON<textarea name="geometryJson" rows="6" placeholder="Paste the image-analysis JSON here, not the original layout plan">{{geometryJson}}</textarea></label>
    <label>Or choose a JSON file (takes priority over pasted text)<input type="file" name="geometryFile" accept=".json,application/json"></label>
    <button type="button" data-action="importGeometry">Import geometry for review</button>
    {{#if hasProposal}}
    <p class="sa-status good">{{geometrySummary}}</p>
    {{#each geometryNotes}}<p class="sa-status warning">{{this}}</p>{{/each}}
    {{#each geometryReview}}<p class="sa-status warning">{{this}}</p>{{/each}}
    <label>Geometry overlay<select name="geometryOverlay"><option value="proposed">Proposed geometry</option><option value="current">Current geometry</option><option value="both">Both</option><option value="none">Artwork only</option></select></label>
    <p class="hint">Proposed walls: mint · Doors: pink · Review markers: dashed orange. Current walls: yellow. Open passages are dashed guides only. Preview again after changing the overlay.</p>
    <label class="sa-check"><input type="checkbox" name="geometryReviewed"> I have reviewed the marked segments and accept them as a starting point.</label>
    <div class="sa-actions"><button type="button" data-action="previewGeometry">Preview geometry</button><button type="button" data-action="applyGeometry">Apply proposed geometry</button></div>
    <div class="sa-geometry-preview"></div>
    <p class="hint">Applying replaces all current walls and doors, including manual edits, and saves the previous walls for restoration. Geometry is estimated from the image and may still need correction.</p>
    {{/if}}
    {{else}}<p class="hint">Apply your complete map background first to enable this step.</p>{{/if}}
    {{#if hasGeometryBackup}}<button type="button" data-action="restoreGeometry">Restore previous walls</button>{{/if}}
  </section>
  <section class="sa-section">
    <h2>5. Refine in Foundry</h2>
    <p>View the scene and use Foundry's wall controls to move wall endpoints, reposition doors or add/remove segments to match the artwork. Adjust lights as needed. Test movement and vision with a player token.</p>
    <p class="hint">The module starts with geometry from the plan; it does not detect walls in the generated image. Reimporting changes only the background and preserves your native edits. Global image alignment cannot correct local changes in room shapes.</p>
    <button type="button" data-action="viewScene">View scene</button>
  </section>
  {{/if}}
</div>
